An **iterator** marks a place in a vector. `begin()` marks the first element and `end()` marks one past the last. `*it` reads the element and `++it` steps on.

```cpp
double total = 0;
for (auto it = px.begin() + 1; it != px.end(); ++it) {
    total += *it;
}
```

